# Docker does not read .gitignore, and Dockerfile's `COPY . .` uploads whatever
# is left here into the daemon's build context. Without this file that means
# .git, .idea/ and a ~13 MB bin/kafka-metrics-agent on every build, which both
# costs upload time and busts the COPY layer cache on commits that touch no Go
# source at all.
#
# Deny-everything-then-allow, rather than a list of things to exclude: the build
# needs exactly four paths and nothing else, so anything added to the repo in
# future -- a fixture directory, a vendored dashboard, a credentials file
# someone drops in by accident -- stays out of the context by default instead of
# having to be remembered here. Adding a new top-level Go source directory does
# require a line below, but the failure mode is a loud "no required module
# provides package" at build time, not a silently fat image.
*

# The dependency layer (`COPY go.mod go.sum ./`) and the compile.
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!internal
